# Valgrind suppressions for KES.
#
# glibc caches a just-joined/detached pthread's stack (including its
# TLS block) internally for reuse rather than immediately unmapping
# it, so Memcheck's leak checker -- which can only prove reachability
# via pointers it can find, not via glibc's own internal free-list --
# conservatively classifies that cached block as "possibly lost". This
# is a well-known, benign Valgrind/glibc interaction (not a real leak:
# the block is still tracked and reusable by glibc, just not reachable
# via a pointer Valgrind's scanner can locate), independent of this
# project's own code. It's suppressed here rather than left for every
# caller of `make valgrind`/`make check-all` to triage by hand each
# time -- see the "Track A.3.1" Resolved entry in PENDING_ITEMS.md for
# how this was found and confirmed to also reproduce against
# pre-fix code, unrelated to any kes_cache.c logic.
{
   glibc_pthread_stack_tls_possibly_lost
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   ...
   fun:allocate_dtv
   fun:_dl_allocate_tls
   fun:allocate_stack
   fun:pthread_create*
}
